1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,125
A business hours calendar says when you are open.

2
00:00:04,125 --> 00:00:08,101
This video shows why it exists, where a calendar is used, how to

3
00:00:08,101 --> 00:00:12,760
create one with a weekly schedule and holidays, and the rules worth knowing.

4
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:20,611
Callers expect a different answer after hours.

5
00:00:20,611 --> 00:00:24,863
A queue that rings agents who have gone home, or a dialer that

6
00:00:24,863 --> 00:00:28,740
calls customers at night, wastes time and annoys people.

7
00:00:29,490 --> 00:00:34,869
Without a shared definition, each queue, phone menu and campaign needs its own

8
00:00:34,869 --> 00:00:39,160
idea of open, and they drift apart when the schedule changes.

9
00:00:39,910 --> 00:00:43,640
A business hours calendar is that shared definition.

10
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:47,370
Change it once, and everything that uses it follows.

11
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:52,417
It handles the weekly schedule, a time zone, and the holidays when you

12
00:00:52,417 --> 00:00:53,830
are closed all day.

13
00:00:58,030 --> 00:01:02,880
A queue uses a calendar to hold or overflow callers while you are closed.

14
00:01:03,630 --> 00:01:08,059
An inbound entry point uses it to pick the closed action:

15
00:01:08,059 --> 00:01:10,660
voicemail, overflow, or reject.

16
00:01:11,410 --> 00:01:15,886
A dialer profile uses it as the outbound calling window, checked in the

17
00:01:15,886 --> 00:01:17,630
contact's own time zone.

18
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:22,991
An automatic activity load uses it, so that AI follow-up messages are only

19
00:01:22,991 --> 00:01:24,720
sent while you are open.

20
00:01:28,926 --> 00:01:33,133
Open Interaction Center, Management, Business hours.

21
00:01:33,133 --> 00:01:34,946
Click Add calendar.

22
00:01:35,398 --> 00:01:40,008
Enter a Name, such as Support hours, and an optional Description.

23
00:01:40,458 --> 00:01:43,713
Pick the Time zone the hours are written in.

24
00:01:43,713 --> 00:01:46,578
When it is empty, the hours are in UTC

25
00:01:47,034 --> 00:01:52,019
In Weekly schedule, tick Open for each open day, and set From and To.

26
00:01:52,019 --> 00:01:56,274
A new calendar starts with Monday to Friday, nine to five.

27
00:01:56,728 --> 00:02:01,483
Close Friday afternoon early by changing its To time, and tick Open on

28
00:02:01,483 --> 00:02:04,048
Saturday for a short morning shift.

29
00:02:04,503 --> 00:02:09,537
In Holidays, enter one date per line, in the form year, month, day.

30
00:02:09,537 --> 00:02:13,123
The calendar is closed all day on those dates.

31
00:02:13,576 --> 00:02:16,211
Leave Enabled ticked, and click Save.

32
00:02:16,211 --> 00:02:22,096
The calendar is listed, and can now be picked on queues, entry points and dialer profiles.

33
00:02:26,296 --> 00:02:28,343
The To time is exclusive.

34
00:02:28,343 --> 00:02:31,646
Nine to five closes at exactly five o'clock.

35
00:02:32,396 --> 00:02:36,476
The same From and To time means open for twenty-four hours.

36
00:02:37,226 --> 00:02:41,460
A To time earlier than the From time runs past midnight, for example

37
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:43,806
ten at night to six in the morning.

38
00:02:44,556 --> 00:02:50,257
Holiday lines that are not valid dates are ignored, so check the list after you save.

39
00:02:50,257 --> 00:02:53,515
And a disabled calendar never closes anything:

40
00:02:53,515 --> 00:02:57,086
every queue that uses it is treated as always open.

41
00:03:01,286 --> 00:03:05,239
A support team opens a queue from eight to six on weekdays.

42
00:03:05,239 --> 00:03:09,496
After hours, callers reach voicemail instead of a ringing phone.

43
00:03:10,246 --> 00:03:14,324
A sales team calls from nine to five in the customer's time zone,

44
00:03:14,324 --> 00:03:18,576
so a customer in another time zone is never called before breakfast.

45
00:03:19,326 --> 00:03:24,324
Holidays are added once, and every queue, menu and campaign that uses the

46
00:03:24,324 --> 00:03:26,476
calendar is closed that day.

47
00:03:27,226 --> 00:03:32,260
A team that sends AI follow-up texts keeps them inside opening hours, so

48
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:34,326
nobody is texted at night.

49
00:03:36,326 --> 00:03:41,094
Define your opening hours once, with their time zone and holidays, and let

50
00:03:41,094 --> 00:03:45,266
queues, phone menus, the dialer and automated texts follow them.

51
00:03:45,266 --> 00:03:46,816
Thanks for watching.

